(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Euclidean infrageometry", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"23f12ee9-3cb6-45d5-9553-97e63ca1cdb7"],

Cell["[[ LLM Generated ]]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"eb65f5ef-daf3-4ef9-8bee-7a19f78401ae"],

Cell["Core definitions", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"e8b1a311-0e43-447d-9c13-e3e6199cd5fc"],

Cell["\<\
The aim is to describe geometric objects on a graph and ask when they \
approach Euclidean objects. Let G = (V, E) be a finite connected simple \
undirected graph with unit edge lengths and shortest-path distance d.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a35ecb6-64f8-4edb-aa7b-ed9f3ea1fc29"],

Cell["Segments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"56a3bafd-eb79-458b-b6c0-bd75e40da2ad"],

Cell["\<\
A segment from p to q is the family of all shortest paths between them. Its \
support is the metric interval:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"76bdd7c8-63f9-4496-8eb5-e38d1ed97b94"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"I", "(", "p", ",", "q", ")", "=", "{", "v", "\[Element]", "V", ":", 
  "d", "(", "p", ",", "v", ")", "+", "d", "(", "v", ",", "q", ")", "=", "d", "(",
   "p", ",", "q", ")", "}"}]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"a745ed33-\
c2e4-4b53-9230-2fa051f1f149"],

Cell["\<\
The distance equality says exactly that a shortest path can pass through v. \
The supporting set is uniquely defined, although the path need not be unique.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fa67dfd8-33fb-4c22-8b12-a11fff5ad55a"],

Cell["Densities and measures", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b9dc05a7-3c74-4593-918b-842b81fbad2d"],

Cell["\<\
Let N be the number of shortest paths, let m = d(p, q), and let c(v) count \
the paths containing v. Under uniform sampling of paths, the probability of \
visiting v is:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aa058eb5-fab7-4c69-9fec-864ab319a450"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", "v", ")", "="}], 
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{"c", "(", "v", ")"}], "N"]}]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"c5580a0c-c15f-44bc-a40f-18e11225d9bb"],

Cell["\<\
Every path visits m + 1 vertices. Counting path\[Dash]vertex incidences in \
two ways therefore gives:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6094f819-8d63-4da2-96c0-674fde258c76"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
   RowBox[{"v", "\[Element]", "V"}]], 
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", "v", ")", "=", "m", "+", "1"}]}]], "DisplayFormula",E\
xpressionUUID->"2731200d-534e-42df-b47c-a20f4f80a5d5"],

Cell["\<\
To obtain a probability measure on the vertices, divide once more by m + 1:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5cd776b0-8a5d-4ee5-a45c-878824d551de"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "=", 
  FractionBox["1", 
   RowBox[{"N", "(", "m", "+", "1", ")"}]], 
  UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
   RowBox[{"v", "\[Element]", "V"}]], 
  RowBox[{"c", "(", "v", ")"}], 
  SubscriptBox["\[Delta]", "v"]}]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"c7e19c43-53ef-4320-b8d6-c77f826c959a"],

Cell["\<\
A limiting segment may carry normalized arclength measure. A Dirac measure at \
the whole segment instead belongs to a space of geometric objects, not to the \
underlying space of points.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77a38d23-f4a6-482d-afa6-6294e15bfb1f"],

Cell["The square grid", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"91bfd384-e9a8-49b8-a94b-61d5fde06393"],

Cell["\<\
From (0, 0) to (a, b), for nonnegative integers a and b, each shortest path \
orders a horizontal and b vertical steps. Thus:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b900885-46f7-4b97-aef9-7de2c450bad7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", "=", 
  RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{"a", "+", "b"}]},
     {"a"}
    }], ")"}]}]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"46b189ff-2287-49dc-8709-\
ad098a34417f"],

Cell["\<\
All vertices in the rectangle belong to the support. In this example, \
stronger edges belong to more shortest paths.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"223d8ac7-b697-4490-9512-20ed315129dc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"vertices", "=", 
     RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "3"}], "]"}], ",", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"pairs", "=", 
     RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
        RowBox[{"vertices", ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"pair", "|->", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Subtract", "@@", "pair"}], "]"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
         "1"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"graph", "=", 
     RowBox[{"Graph", "[", 
      RowBox[{"vertices", ",", 
       RowBox[{"UndirectedEdge", "@@@", "pairs"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"VertexCoordinates", "\[Rule]", "vertices"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}],
    ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"paths", "=", 
     RowBox[{"FindPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{"graph", ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", "6", "}"}], ",", "All"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"counts", "=", 
     RowBox[{"Counts", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Catenate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"path", "|->", 
         RowBox[{"UndirectedEdge", "@@@", 
          RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
           RowBox[{"path", ",", "2", ",", "1"}], "]"}]}]}], "/@", "paths"}], 
       "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Graph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"graph", ",", 
     RowBox[{"EdgeStyle", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"edge", ",", "count"}], "}"}], "|->", 
         RowBox[{"edge", "\[Rule]", 
          RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", 
             FractionBox["count", 
              RowBox[{"Length", "[", "paths", "]"}]], "]"}], ",", "Thick"}], 
           "]"}]}]}], ",", "counts"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",Exp\
ressionUUID->"a19f28e4-e20b-40b7-bcf0-155132eada69"],

Cell["\<\
Rescaling a nearest-neighbor square grid preserves Manhattan distance; it \
does not yield the Euclidean metric. A thin averaged path is therefore \
insufficient evidence of Euclidean geometry.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"71f46bff-ba02-48cd-b2cf-9178a834054a"],

Cell["Main question", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8ed9895b-2581-48d3-a16f-09d2b071deb6"],

Cell["\<\
Which graph sequences, distance scales and sampling laws make these \
constructions converge to their Euclidean counterparts? Start with segments \
and a precise bound comparing graph distances with Euclidean distances.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b4979cc-8a71-4bcb-a3a6-170d23280750"],

Cell["\<\
Prepared with Codex from the Euclidean Infrageometry guide, 7 November 2026. \
The project attributes the research direction to Stephen Wolfram. The \
original guide is unchanged.\
\>", "SmallText",ExpressionUUID->"4e2ab1b6-8147-43db-bbb7-390fa2d99bea"]
},
Saveable->True,
WindowTitle->"Euclidean infrageometry",
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
